# Full accepted example compilation preparation

**The remaining-context correction is ready for focused review, then serialized coordinator retry.**
Consumer-first failed restore (NU1510); consumer-second restored, reached Csc and failed on generated
imports. Consumer-third cleared those imports, then emitted 21 remaining generated-context diagnostics.
All three attempts remain failed; there is no accepted Full compilation. No example/test execution has run.
The 17-body A/C pilot already passed its genuine clean
compile at accepted-compilation SHA-256
`4b17d3e629b608b9a8b127696a9cbaa26c53b31523589a81c89e00f45b3531d6`.
Its source/manifest/wrappers/tools/records remain exact; it is not rerun for bookkeeping.

## Accepted population and dispositions

The current [manifest](validation/examples/full/manifest-contexts-fixed.json) joins the accepted A/C pilot,
protocol, transport, FIDO, SHARED, five-applet, PGP/PIV and external revision-4 inventories/reviews:

| Population | Disposition |
| --- | --- |
| 41 pilot records | 17 compiled checkpoint bodies, two qualified internal illustrations and 22 historical exclusions; original proof stays unchanged. |
| 415 additional accepted main-batch records | Current exact source regions/body hashes reconciled with revision-2 authorities; two corrected PIV Markdown bodies included. |
| 247 external authority records | All accepted classification-overlay replacements verified; current source regions stay separate from original base/historical records. |
| **703 total authority records** | Every record has an explicit source/version/classification and compilation/execution disposition. |
| **302 additional prepared occurrences** | **300 distinct source/context compilations**: 244 consumer bodies plus 58 real-test-context occurrences / 56 unique test-context bodies. Two exact same-body/same-real-context aliases avoid duplicate compilation. |
| **34 review-accepted qualifications** | Explicit partial design, rejected pattern, generated/XML excerpt, internal contributor or fixture-dependent scaffold; unchanged source-backed rationale per ID, confirmed by the original Full review. |
| Other nonparticipants | Shell/JSON/layout/output/diagram and actual historical material; no C# or runtime credit. |

The manifest retains exact raw XML/fence bytes, line/byte boundaries, source/body hashes, author
inventory and review hashes. Current After regions in mixed Before/After fences remain eligible:
`FULL-047` and `FULL-165` compile their current After portions with exact historical Before subranges
preserved. Explicit secret-logging/allocation antipatterns are separated from the prepared recommended
portions. The external overlay keeps its obsolete invalid IYubiKeyFilter base separate from the repaired
current real filter/test body; JSON and XML-embedded shell recipes are not relabelled C#.

`qualification-decisions.json` lists all 34 proposed non-compilation qualifications individually. In
particular, elided MAC/parser/reset/device-reader behavior is never supplied by a dummy helper. The
current LibraryImport declaration needs both internal access and an unsafe-enabled owning context:
Core.UnitTests has the IVT but not that language setting. Its policy is left unchanged, with the
contributor declaration explicitly qualified instead of broadening SDK/root/test policy. This worker's
proposal is not independent final coverage acceptance. A reviewer-requested additional genuine context
remains a bounded correction before release.

## Real contexts and unchanged compilation pattern

The new consumer library is `Yubico.YubiKit.Audit20261111.DocExamples.Full.csproj`, non-packable and
without an entry point. Its filename avoids Core and unit/resilience selector collisions. It references
the actual SDK modules, Cli.Shared and the actual public PivTool/ManagementTool helpers, rather than
copying SDK/sample implementation. Framework/Hosting/Console references supply the actual documented
hosting and ASP.NET contexts. The current Serilog application example uses explicit audit-only package
versions selected from public NuGet metadata: Hosting **10.0.0**, Console **6.1.1**, File **7.0.0**.
Exact `.nuspec` sources and selection rationale are retained under `application-dependencies/`.
Repository central/shipping package configuration is unchanged; restore/assets/Csc evidence remains
required from the actual build.

Test examples use compile-only `Compile` injection into **nine actual existing projects**, with their
real xUnit version, fixture types, helper imports and existing IVT. There is no impersonated assembly
name, new access grant, copied SDK implementation or product project edit. Public test/filter types,
the actual internal Core fakes and the actual CTAP/WebAuthn test helpers supply their genuine contexts.
The documented current factory/credential/response/connection/prompt scopes stay intact. Arrays cleared
by original finally blocks receive actual mutable dedicated-buffer parameters, not read-only memory.

The targeted hook repeats the qualified pilot's late-CoreCompile pattern and loads its source-pinned
compiler observer for exact Csc source/reference/analyzer/config/file-input membership and
implementation/reference/PDB proof. The Full-owned adapter changes only its single descriptor call site
to pass the selected actual project explicitly. The proven parser runs with a private function-global
copy for that project; the qualified module's PROJECT/ROOT and all captured raw arguments stay unchanged.
Context/source membership and approved output ownership remain explicit. The qualified comma/quote-aware file parser and v2 logger are loaded read-only at their pinned
hashes. No NuGet graph interpreter, compiler-proof version stack or new supervisor is introduced.

Static inspection caught the real extra xUnit v3 inputs before any build: the package's
`DefaultRunnerReporters.cs` plus `SelfRegisteredExtensions.cs` and `XunitAutoGeneratedEntryPoint.cs` in
the two unit contexts. Their actual package targets/task identities and before-Csc source hashes are
bound; unmatched source additions still fail. The existing SDK Source Link/embedded-input producers
precede capture. Actual policy is recorded per project; Recommended test policy is not called
AllEnabledByDefault, and actual canonical analyzer DLL participation is checked without assuming the
SDK's duplicate-analyzer flag remains enabled.

**No test/example DLL is executed.** Audit test declarations exist only in those compile outputs.
After all compile proofs are preserved, the final ordinary clean solution build must restore normal
uninjected test outputs **before any SDK test lane**. The wrapper's injection environment lives only in
its child process; no product file is changed.

## Outputs and preserved originals

- The accepted pilot's **29** mutable local compiler inputs/outputs (**4,015,574 bytes**) were copied
  before later builds, with exact original-path/hash-to-copy mappings in `pilot-output-preservation.json`.
  Installed SDK/framework/NuGet caches and reconstructible source corpus were excluded.
- The Full consumer host alone uses dedicated
  `/home/rupicola/Code/y/.core-docs-audit-runtime/core-001/jobs/<project-name>/{bin,obj}`.
- Referenced SDK/current tool projects and the real selected test projects use their ordinary primary
  ignored `bin/obj` trees. This extends the coordinator's explicit ordinary-primary build scope; no
  `/tmp`, other-worktree or frozen-archive output is selected. Actual paths are observed, not substituted.
  The declared full reference closure contains 25 real projects.
- Every successful context preserves only its needed mutable local compiled outputs/references and
  generated compiler inputs immediately under `core-001/full-example-preservation/<label>/`, with a
  textual exact mapping retained in its attempt. It avoids copying unconsumed dependency/native assets
  or global caches. Final own DLL/PDB/reference and dependency/runtime metadata have explicit roles.
- Context proofs distinguish original exact retained outputs from later overwritten paths. They infer
  no binary/runtime equivalence and never rebuild an old context merely to repair bookkeeping.

