## Coordinator commands after acceptance

Load the current build skill and serialize within the primary checkout. First verify the prepared
records, then compile the consumer context as the first broad representative:

```bash
F=docs/research/documentation-audit/modules/core/pass-1/core-001/validation/examples/full
P=3e40cb440ddd872de8bfba3ae3c0e45166ff5dbcb3a44aad890b968c97885228
python3 -B "$F/verify.py"
python3 -B "$F/run.py" --context consumer --label examples-full-consumer-fourth \
  --profile "$F/reviewed-inputs-contexts-fixed.json" --profile-sha256 "$P"
```

The actual command is canonical:

```bash
dotnet toolchain.cs -- build --project Yubico.YubiKit.Audit20261111.DocExamples.Full --clean
```

After its successful complete zero-warning receipt and actual captures are accepted, use the same
wrapper/profile serially for the actual existing test contexts:

| `--context` | Fresh `--label` | Canonical `--project` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Core.UnitTests` | `examples-full-core-unit-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.Core.UnitTests` |
| `Ctap2.UnitTests` | `examples-full-ctap-unit-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.UnitTests` |
| `Ctap2.IntegrationTests` | `examples-full-ctap-integration-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2.IntegrationTests` |
| `Management.IntegrationTests` | `examples-full-management-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.Management.IntegrationTests` |
| `SecurityDomain.IntegrationTests` | `examples-full-security-domain-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.SecurityDomain.IntegrationTests` |
| `Piv.IntegrationTests` | `examples-full-piv-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.Piv.IntegrationTests` |
| `Core.IntegrationTests` | `examples-full-core-integration-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.Core.IntegrationTests` |
| `WebAuthn.IntegrationTests` | `examples-full-webauthn-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.WebAuthn.IntegrationTests` |
| `Oath.IntegrationTests` | `examples-full-oath-first` | `Yubico.YubiKit.Oath.IntegrationTests` |

For example:

```bash
python3 -B "$F/run.py" --context Core.UnitTests --label examples-full-core-unit-first \
  --profile "$F/reviewed-inputs-contexts-fixed.json" --profile-sha256 "$P"
```

The wrapper always runs `dotnet toolchain.cs -- build --project <that exact stem> --clean`, never a test
target. Require successful actual exit, complete streams/retention/quiescence, zero warnings/errors,
nonempty real Csc arguments, exact membership, unchanged before inputs, matching compiler/final outputs
and successful immediate preservation. Acceptance records live only in `full/attempts/<label>/`; actual
qualified logger records remain in `validation/commands-v2/<label>/`. Keep every first failure and use
fresh labels after reviewed corrections. The original pilot selector/attempt is historical and is not
rerun now that the Full project exists.

Final token/API/repository/docs/package/architecture/complexity gates and normal test rebuild/run remain
coordinator-owned. Native/platform/physical qualification, PIV physical deferral and Windows late handoff
remain separate. Finish Core Pass 1 publication and the deferred-finding handoff, then stop.
